                                                                         1/3
"B" commands:

Extended letter commands:

     These commands are shortcuts for creating various items.  They should
     normally be followed by 2 or 3 numbers (parameters 2, 3, 4).

         box 3 45 14   will put a box on staff 3 at position 45,
                       vertical position 14.
BAR   = barline
BARn  = barline, n = number of staves up
BARBC = "curvy" brace
BARBK = bracket
BARD  = double bar
BARH  = heavy double bar
BARL  = repeat bar, dots to left
BARR  = repeat bar, dots to right
BARRD = double repeat bar, dots on both sides
BAS   = bass clef (BASSM = mini clef)
BEAM  = single beam
BEAMn = beam, n = number of beams
BOX   = box

*
                                                                         2/3
************** GROUP EDIT BOXES ***************

DRAWING BOXES TO SET COPY, MOVE, DELETE, ETC. AREAS:

The main Command mode menu has a GROUP box. Clicking on this box brings
up the Group Edit menu. Click on ? to get explanations of the various
abbreviations in the boxes.

The Group Edit commands lead to a prompt regarding setting the limits 
of the material to be processed. The limits may be set by typing numbers
defining the lower staff number, the left position, the right position,
the upper staff number, and the type of item (Code number).

If the mouse is used to define the limits, the following considerations
should be made. The box is drawn by holding down the left button as the
mouse is moved. You will see above the graphics window a text line which
gives an account of the changing position of the cursor.

    Lower Staff  n1  x1    Upper Staff  n2  x2




*
                                                                         3/3

The specific heights of the horizontal box lines are important only in
regard to the vertical staff positions. The vertical position numbers,
n1 and n2, only refer to staff numbers. If a horizontal line is out of
the range of any staff (i.e. between staves), the number will appear
as ****. The horizontal numbers, x1 and x2, are based on the normal SCORE
horizontal spacing steps. Clicking in the middle of the box allows you
to move the entire box to a new position.

VERY IMPORTANT: If the width of the box (x2-x1) is less than 5
steps it is interpreted as including the entire width of a normal line,
from position 0 to 200. Thus a single click on a staff can select that
line for copying, moving, etc. To select the entire width of a group of
staves, a thin vertical box should be drawn extending from the lowest
staff to the highest to be included.

After the box is created a list of code numbers will appear at the bottom
of the screen. You may choose any single number or, you may choose zero,
in which case all code numbers will be affected.



